    "baseRefName": "staging",
    "body": "## Summary\nAuthor the governance artifacts the verifier flagged as absent: the risk→control matrix (`controls.md`), machine-readable and human data inventories, system/device inventories, data-flow map, data-handling policy, the AI/Agent-Use policy, SEV definitions, and the AUP AI clause. Also record policy approvals: under the solo coder-agent / reviewer-agent / human-signer model, approval = the signer merging through the gate, so every policy's `approved_by` is set to the accountable signer.\n\n## Tickets\n| Ticket | Title | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| #22 | Governance artifacts: control matrix, data inventories, AI policy | In Progress |\n\n## Changes\n- compliance/data-inventory.yaml\n- docs/data-flows.md\n- evidence/vendors/README.md\n- inventory/devices.yaml\n- inventory/systems.md\n- policies/acceptable-use-policy.md\n- policies/access-control.md\n- policies/ai-agent-use.md\n- policies/bcdr.md\n- policies/change-management.md\n- policies/code-of-conduct.md\n- policies/controls.md\n- policies/data-classification.md\n- policies/data-handling.md\n- policies/data-retention.md\n- policies/encryption.md\n- policies/governance.md\n- policies/incident-response.md\n- policies/information-security.md\n- policies/logging-and-monitoring.md\n- policies/objectives-and-commitments.md\n- policies/onboarding-offboarding.md\n- policies/people-security.md\n- policies/physical-security.md\n- policies/privacy.md\n- policies/processing-integrity.md\n- policies/risk-management.md\n- policies/risk-register.md\n- policies/role-matrix.md\n- policies/roles-and-responsibilities.md\n- policies/security-training.md\n- policies/vendor-management.md\n- policies/vulnerability-and-deficiency-management.md\n- policies/vulnerability-management.md\n- runbooks/incident-response.md\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] Docs/YAML only — no source files, no unit tests required by the gate\n- [x] `controls.md` maps every risk (R1–R8) to controls and criteria; `risk-register.md` references them\n- [x] All policy frontmatter now carries `approved_by: dorkalev` + `approved_at` (approval = this merge)\n- [x] Data inventory + data-flows + device roster present for CC6.4/CC6.7 checks",
